	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "b7f2b5b0-6b6b-4f5a-9a7a-3f5a2f0e9d11",
		"name": "Field Service Platform - Backend API",
		"description": "Data-seeding and manual-testing collection for the Spring Boot backend.\n\nTypical flow:\n1. Set `owner_phone` / `owner_pin` (collection variables) to your bootstrap owner credentials from `backend/.env`, then run **Auth > Login - Owner**. This saves the JWT into `owner_token` automatically.\n2. Run **Owner - Workers > Create Worker** to add a worker (saves the new id into `worker_id`).\n3. Run **Owner - Projects > Create Project** (saves `project_id`), then **Owner - Sites > Create Site** (saves `site_id`).\n4. Run **Owner - Assignments > Create Assignment** to link the worker to that site.\n5. Run **Auth > Login - Worker** using the phone/pin you gave the worker in step 2 (edit `new_worker_phone`/`new_worker_pin` request body first if you changed them) \u2014 saves `worker_token`.\n6. Use the **Worker - ...** folders to clock in/out, manage availability, and view timesheets as that worker.\n\nAll IDs and tokens are stored as collection variables and chained automatically by each request's test script \u2014 you normally don't need to copy/paste anything by hand.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
